  GEnie        FIGSURVEY        Page  ???
       Forth Interest Group Survey

   1. Instructions
   2. Take the Survey

  Enter #, <P>revious, or <H>elp?1

  The Forth Interest Group Survey has been designed for the purpose of providing
  FIG a better understanding of the needs of our members, and to provide us
  feedback about some of the pressing issues concerning the Forth Language.

  The FIG Survey consists of 20 multiple choice questions. At the end of each
  question, you will be prompted for an answer. Please choose the letter which
  appears before your answer. On questions that may allow more than one answer,
  you may choose to enter a group of letters separated by commas, as in A,B,C, 
or
  by placing a space between each letter, as in A B C, or by simply stringing 
the
  letters together, as in ABC. Any of the above choices will record your answers
  correctly. The last question gives you the option to provide further comment 
to
  FIG via GE Mail.

  At any point during the Survey, you may exit without recording your answers by
  typing QUIT.  You may skip any question by pressing <RETURN> at the answer
  prompt.  After you have completed the survey, you may answer just the skipped
  questions, or answer all questions by taking the survey again.

  The Forth Interest Group thanks you for your time and participation in the
  Survey and in helping us to continue to offer a high quality service.


  GEnie        FIGSURVEY        Page  ???
       Forth Interest Group Survey

   1. Instructions
   2. Take the Survey

  Enter #, <P>revious, or <H>elp?2

  There are 20 total questions in this survey. Some questions require one 
answer,
  others allow multiple answers.  You will have a chance to send comments
  following the survey.  To skip a question, simply press <RETURN> at the 
prompt.
  To end the survey, type STOP.

